cute). Retain settings already supplied by\\n28: the user; do not call a separate intent-classification model. Do not silently\\n29: choose a worker count from defaults or `auto`; obtain a positive integer or\\n30: the user's explicit confirmation of a proposed number. N bounds local R-node\\n31: reviews and, in a separate phase, local Lean proofs. NL0/Audit A and\\n32: Lean preparation/proofs/assembly/Audit B have separate phase profiles. The user\\n33: does not prepare queues, task packets or controller jobs manually.\\n34: The invoking owner follows [foreground handoff and monitoring](nl0/references/owner-observation.md):\\n35: normally dispatch with `--detach`, verify the owned processes, and register one\\n36: host heartbeat for a bounded check every ten minutes. Record the actual schedule\\n37: ID, report that mathematical work is still pending, then end the current\\n38: foreground turn. Never keep the owner active through sleep/poll loops. Each\\n39: scheduled check ends its turn as well. `DISPATCHED` is not workflow completion.\\n40: If host scheduling is unavailable, disclose that and return manual status/cancel\\n41: commands; do not claim that a monitor was registered. Frozen author/proof/reviewer\\n42: stages perform only their assigned roles and never schedule owner monitoring or\\n43: redispatch the workflow.\\n44: \\n45: For missing external originals, follow [ordered source retrieval](nl0/references/source-retrieval.md):\\n46: arXiv, Google full-text search, Google DOI discovery, then confirmed-DOI Sci-Hub\\n47: lookup with ordinary browser readback when needed. Reuse an already available\\n48: adequate primary source; retrieval alone does not establish theorem fidelity.\\n49: At invocation disclose the [conditional-source policy](nl0/references/conditional-sources.md):\\n50: inaccessible primary texts can permit continued work from complete explicit\\n51: secondary statements, but the final result remains conditional. Show each\\n52: actual warning