empts mechanical\\n126:    [assembly and source-facing export](nl02lean/references/assembly.md).\\n127:    Use the serial connection author only for actual connection/library-discharge\\n128:    repair. Normal final machine Audit B inherits the frozen semantic review;\\n129:    B-final is reserved for proof-valid interface deviation.\\n130:    Use\\n131:    `nl02lean/scripts/source_preparation.py` for bounded shared extraction,\\n132:    then `workflow.py` for source/IR freeze, proof work and final gates.\\n133: 3. **Full workflow.** Complete track one, then track two. A changed mathematical\\n134:    statement or new theorem returns to the affected NL0/Audit A boundary.\\n135: \\n136: ## Mathematical invariants\\n137: \\n138: - Accepted NL0 is a complete natural-language proof relative to explicit H/E/M,\\n139:   fixed logic and its hash-bound verified background supplement. Important\\n140:   tools remain explicit; ordinary correct elementary reasoning needs no\\n141:   exhaustive calculation chain. See [background notes](nl0/references/background-notes.md).\\n142: - Within NL0, each inference uses only its direct inputs, global definitions and explicitly\\n143:   established in-scope local facts or positively checked node-local background\\n144:   notes. Notes never add H or repair a substantive gap. Source papers and producer proof bodies do\\n145:   not fill gaps in a task packet.\\n146: - Preserve one global mathematical identity while allowing local Lean views.\\n147:   Actual cross-view conversions need checked proofs. In stage two, the pinned\\n148:   Mathlib environment is freely available without NL0 M registration.\\n149: - Shared mathematical extraction is a bounded local change at translation entry.\\n150:   Review its new producer and substitution cuts; inherit unchanged evidence.\\n151:   Freeze the revised NL0 before final IR and worker packets.\\n152: - Local conditional bodies may run concurrently. Assembly must discharge every\\n153:   internal dependency with an actual checked proof; conditional checks alone\\n154:   are not a final result.\\n155: - The independent pre-freeze review checks every E and complete P, including\\n156:   hypotheses, quantifiers and relevant definitions. Final machine Audit B checks\\n157:   actual exported full types and complete closure against that frozen authority.\\n158:   Supply short direct/equivalent correspondence explanations. Check actual Lean\\n159:   closure and trust, without a Mathlib-to-NL0 use ledger.\\n160:   Neither author notes nor a compiler pass are semantic approval.\\n161: - Stop on a judged substantive mathematical gap. Ordinary expansion and local\\n162:   verifiable corrections remain allowed. Difficulty or elapsed time does not\\n163:   establish that a mathematical claim is false.\\n164: \\n165: ## Clean execution and accounting\\n166: \\n167: Operators use [execution terminology](nl0/references/terminology.md) to distinguish\\n168: Codex conversations, native subagents, Yui jobs, worker slots and controllers.\\n169: Use the logical phase names **NL0 worker**, **preprocessing worker**,\\n170: **formalization workers (N slots)** and **postprocessing worker**. A logical\\n171: worker may contain several separate author/reviewer threads and program steps;\\n172: N limits concurrent local R reviews and local Lean proof jobs in their separate phases.\\n173: Report executor termination separately from mathematical acceptance.\\n174: \\n175: Read [isolation](nl0/references/isolation.md) and [measurement](nl0/references/measurement.md)\\n176: before any model test or benchmark. Run model authoring, planning, proof and\\n177: review stages through the isolated carrier. The interactive developer's memory,\\n178: other personal skills, expert packages, old task outputs and hidden reference\\n179: proofs are never an input source for these stages.\\n180: \\n181: The Yui arm receives only the declared Yui rules and task material. The direct\\n182: arm receives a minimal task/tool contract and the same mathematical inputs,\\n183: without Yui planning, strategy or shared-proof guidance. Log controller-supplied instructions, frozen inputs, native configuration,\\n184: tool schemas/results, reported model identity, phase, usage and health. Native\\n185: Codex manages model networking and context; Yui does not intercept HTTP payloads.\\n186: Actual tier and per-response usage coverage remain unknown when not exposed. Never execute model-generated Python or shell text.\\n187: \\n188: Collect the active phase profiles as described above. `config.json` supplies\\n189: defaults only when explicitly selected. The current isolated native Codex carrier requests\\n190: Standard speed and checks model/effort availability without fallback. Freeze\\n191: and record each stage's selected profile;\\n192: never silently substitute a stronger model or fallback.\\n193: Resolve the confirmed concurrency before dispatch and record its basis; do not\\n194: claim an unknown backend maximum. N limits local R-node reviews, then local\\n195: Lean proof jobs in a later phase. NL0 authoring, global Audit A, preparation,\\n196: interface work, assembly and Audit B use one serial lane per case.\\n197: Count root/controller, worker, review and retry calls. Cached/reasoning tokens\\n198: are subsets of input/output totals, not extra tokens. Missing usage is unknown.\\n199: \\n200: Return the exact accepted scope, source/formal artifacts, unresolved citations\"}"}
{"i":2,"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"path\": \"nl0/references/audit-a.md\", \"total_lines\": 377, \"start\": 1, \"end\": 250, \"start_column\": 0, \"end_column\": 0, \"requested_end\": 250, \"has_more\": true, \"next_start\": 251, \"next_column\": 0, \"next_end\": 377, \"text\": \"1: # Audit A: per-object natural-language verification\\n2: \\n3: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:begin -->\\n4: ## Shared mathematical acceptance requirements\\n5: \\n6: Contract version: `nl0-audit-a-8`.\\n7: \\n8: This section is the single authority for what an accepted NL0 must satisfy.\\n9: Authoring instructions explain how to meet it; the audit checks these same\\n10: requirements. The table IDs also name executable coverage groups. Detailed\\n11: definitions in self-containment, logical rules and external-theorem review are\\n12: annexes to these requirements, not alternative permission policies.\\n13: \\n14: | ID | Review group | Author evidence group | Requirement |\\n15: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n16: | `target` | package | original_context_note | Preserve the original target, every original H, quantifier, domain, range, normalization, endpoint and supplied core proof route. Parameters name ambient data; they cannot hide an H or a desired conclusion. |\\n17: | `definitions` | package | original_context_note | Give each global object one complete typed definition and each local object a legitimate scoped introduction. Prove or directly assume every construction guard before use. Defining an object grants none of its properties. |\\n18: | `sources` | package | original_context_note | Every selected M/E has an explicit faithful full statement and verified primary/native identity, context and hypotheses. Native typeclass premises are mathematical premises too. Record inaccessible checks as UNVERIFIED; they do not support an unqualified whole-proof pass. |\\n19: | `structure` | package | original_context_note | H/E/M are the only proposition roots. Every N/P has one producer, every reta